# Title: ServiceDll Hijack
# ID: 612e47e9-8a59-43a6-b404-f48683f45bd6
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: frack113
# Date: 2022-02-04
# Tags: attack.persistence, attack.privilege-escalation, attack.t1543.003
# Description: Detects changes to the "ServiceDLL" value related to a service in the registry.
# This is often used as a method of persistence.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((registry_key_name="*\\System\\*" AND registry_key_name="*ControlSet*" AND registry_key_name="*\\Services\\*") AND registry_key_name="*\\Parameters\\ServiceDll") AND NOT (((process_path="C:\\Windows\\system32\\lsass.exe" AND registry_key_name="*\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters\\ServiceDll" AND Details="%%systemroot%%\\system32\\ntdsa.dll") OR (process_path="C:\\Windows\\System32\\poqexec.exe") OR (Details="C:\\Windows\\system32\\spool\\drivers\\x64\\3\\PrintConfig.dll") OR (process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe" AND registry_key_name="*\\Services\\PrintNotify\\Parameters\\ServiceDll" AND Details="C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\DriverStore\\FileRepository\\*" AND Details="*\\arm64\\PrintConfig.dll"))) AND NOT ((process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe" AND Details="C:\\Windows\\System32\\STAgent.dll")))
